    "result_text": "Tests remain green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nI **agreed with the finding** and fixed it. `FlagPossibleDuplicate` now routes both telephones through a `normalizedTelephone(Owner)` helper that calls `OwnerTelephones.toE164(...)` with the same raw-value fallback `OwnerIdentity` uses, instead of the bespoke `telephone.equals(existing.getTelephone())`. This keeps the soft-duplicate comparison consistent with the hard-duplicate path (`RejectDuplicateIdentity`/`OwnerIdentity`): a future change to telephone-normalization semantics in `OwnerTelephones` now flows through this step too, and stored values predating the pipeline compare correctly.\n\nThe new owner's telephone is already E.164 by this point, so for the acceptance test the result is identical \u2014 unique telephones still differ \u2014 and behaviour is unchanged.\n\nOn the **minor point**, the reviewer agreed no change was needed to the `matchId` min-tracking loop (it matches the `for`-loop style in `RejectDuplicateIdentity`), so I left it as is.",
